※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4710
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4710 LANG_ARRAY_NOT_COPIED

※ An array is copied by copying its elements' bytes, which is a copy only of an
※ element that is all of its value.  Text points into room something else
※ keeps, and a second holder of that room is the question the allocator rules
※ answer one value at a time.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let a: mut str⟦2⟧ = ⟦"a", "b"⟧
    let b: mut str⟦2⟧ = ⟦"c", "d"⟧
    a ← b
    if #a⟦0⟧ = 1: 0u6 else: 1u6
